== SZ-1: margin number + why ==
tests/conftest.py run_probe_script default timeout 300 -> 900.
WHY 900: SZ-1 measured the golden leg at 6m10s WALL (370s) with only 3.8s user
CPU — the leg is scheduler-bound, so wall scales with box load (steady 14–20
here, nproc 14). 900s = ~2.4x the measured worst leg: survives a load-20 burst
(~1.5x of load-11 ≈ 560s) with slack, while a genuinely HUNG probe still fails
inside one pytest pass (the 5 engine legs on the worst-case path add <= 75min of
timeout headroom, and only fire when a probe actually hangs). The 5 load-fragile
legs (test_sim_golden x3, test_hub_scroll engine legs x2) all route through
run_probe_script with NO explicit timeout override (VERIFIED: test_sim_golden.py:79-80,
test_hub_scroll.py:414-415) — one number fixes all of them. Rationale is in the
function docstring, not only here.

== D-1 verification (formulas ARE equal — merge permitted) ==
sprite_bank.gd:118  s.scale = Vector3.ONE * (world_h / (float(tex.get_height()) / 100.0))
fx_director.gd:197  s.scale = Vector3.ONE * (h        / (float(tex.get_height()) / 100.0))
Same expression; h/world_h are per-call world-height args. texture_for(id) rides
the tier=1 default and the 4 fx_* ids are NOT in TIER_TEXTURES, so
texture_for(fx_id) == make_sprite's lookup byte-for-byte (VERIFIED:
sprite_bank.gd:79-85 keys = ballista/bombard/hailspire_tower only). Node props
(texture, billboard, scale, order) identical; null-case returns {} as before.
REUSE: _spawn_fx now calls SPRITE_BANK.make_sprite(fx_id, h) — the ONE factory.

